# nr-office-design-xlsx: what the wiring applies for the xlsx design expansion of mixdog-office-design.
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change: the module is pure and has no caller yet; its caller
# is the design system of the later composition task, which names expand_xlsx_sheet.)

# 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/src/lib.rs: add the module after the line `pub mod tokens;`
pub mod xlsx;

# 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/Cargo.toml, [dependencies]: add after the line
#    `mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }`
#    (the module writes the sheet's source citation with mixdog_ooxml::opc::provenance_citation, the one the portable
#    package writes; mixdog-ooxml depends on mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml-text and the zip
#    and hash crates, none of them on mixdog-office-design, so the edge closes no cycle)
mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }

# 3. native/core/Cargo.lock: `cargo update --workspace --offline` adds mixdog-ooxml to the dependencies of the package
#    mixdog-office-design (a workspace member already in the lock; no new external crate and no new feature of one).
#    native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml: `cargo hakari generate` (no third-party dependency is added).

# 4. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; this one goes after the "office-*" sets that sort before it):
    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-xlsx.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-xlsx/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "a12da440f30f981ce88ba2e6df3a5595fb0a2ffae2a40b8e231e8f9c9d8382aa",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-xlsx.mjs",
      "set": "office-xlsx",
      "totalBytes": 1684740
    },

# 5. Two small helpers of this module stand beside ones that tasks of the same wave write; whichever lands second
#    removes its copy and calls the other (the owner's rule: one implementation):
#    - xlsx/mod.rs `korean_design` is `koreanDesign` of design/docx/document-typography.mjs: nr-office-design-docx
#      writes it as docx/typography.rs. After both are in, delete `korean_design` (and its test) from xlsx/mod.rs and call
#      the docx one (pass `design` and the operation's JSON text exactly as expand_xlsx_sheet does now).
#    - xlsx/sheet.rs `display_width` is `displayWidth` of portable/portable-sheet-xml.mjs: nr-office-ooxml-sheet-xml
#      writes it in mixdog-ooxml (sheet_xml.rs). After both are in, delete `display_width` and `is_wide` from
#      xlsx/sheet.rs and call that one (it returns a width in character cells; sheet.rs wants an f64).
